Wine 10.0 Mac driver: give a game its focus back when macOS gives the window focus.

Highball's default engines (x64-sikarugir10.0_6, the main line and the GPTK 4 line) are Gcenx's
Sikarugir build of Wine 10.0, which has no public source for this revision, so these changes ship as
three byte edits to its winemac.so (Scripts/build-winemac-focus.sh makes the file from the published
tarball and checks every byte it touches). This file is the same change in source form, against
wine-10.0's dlls/winemac.drv.

1. window.c, macdrv_window_got_focus: upstream b568eaac4a (wine-10.6, Wine bug 48121). Wine 10 sent
   the game a made-up WM_MOUSEACTIVATE with a non-client hit (HTMENU) before activating it. Unity
   treats that as a click that started in the title bar and ignores the focus gain that follows, so
   after Cmd+Tab, a click on another app or a Dock restore the game kept drawing but dropped every
   click and key (highball#182).

2. and 3. cocoa_window.m, makeFocused and windowDidBecomeKey: CrossOver Hack #18896, as CrossOver
   26.3 ships it. When Wine itself made a window key (a game calling SetFocus on a window that is
   not the foreground one, which Heartopia's Unity player does at start), the driver dropped the
   focus event macOS sent back, so the window was key on the Mac while Wine kept another window as
   foreground. Raw input only reaches the foreground window, so such a game started with a dead
   mouse. With these, the event reaches Wine and the window becomes the foreground.

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
@@ -2130,8 +2130,8 @@
         [self makeKeyWindow];
         causing_becomeKeyWindow = nil;
 
-        [queue discardEventsMatchingMask:event_mask_for_type(WINDOW_GOT_FOCUS) |
-                                         event_mask_for_type(WINDOW_LOST_FOCUS)
+        /* CrossOver Hack #18896: don't discard WINDOW_GOT_FOCUS events */
+        [queue discardEventsMatchingMask:event_mask_for_type(WINDOW_LOST_FOCUS)
                                forWindow:self];
     }
 
@@ -2907,7 +2907,7 @@
         if (event)
             [self flagsChanged:event];
 
-        if (causing_becomeKeyWindow == self) return;
+        /* CrossOver Hack #18896: don't return here based on causing_becomeKeyWindow */
 
         [controller windowGotFocus:self];
     }
diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
@@ -1899,17 +1899,9 @@
 
     if (can_window_become_foreground(hwnd) && !(style & WS_MINIMIZE))
     {
-        /* simulate a mouse click on the menu to find out
-         * whether the window wants to be activated */
-        LRESULT ma = send_message(hwnd, WM_MOUSEACTIVATE,
-                                  (WPARAM)NtUserGetAncestor(hwnd, GA_ROOT),
-                                  MAKELONG(HTMENU, WM_LBUTTONDOWN));
-        if (ma != MA_NOACTIVATEANDEAT && ma != MA_NOACTIVATE)
-        {
-            TRACE("setting foreground window to %p\n", hwnd);
-            NtUserSetForegroundWindow(hwnd);
-            return;
-        }
+        TRACE("setting foreground window to %p\n", hwnd);
+        NtUserSetForegroundWindow(hwnd);
+        return;
     }
 
     TRACE("win %p/%p rejecting focus\n", hwnd, event->window);
